# Matome Base Components — Design-System Catalog (drift guard)

```elixir
# Kino ships with Livebook; no Mix.install needed.
alias Kino.HTML
```

## What this is

A **dev-only** visual catalog of the Matome **base-tier** components (W1 #1869),
the server-side HEEx port of the Flutter `flutter_widgetbook` `Components/Atoms/*`
tier. It is the sibling of `foundations_catalog.livemd` (which covers the raw
tokens) and renders each component's variants in **Light + Dark** so the `/admin`
back-office design system can be eyeballed against the Flutter client.

**Drift-guard chain:**

```
apps/flutter/lib/ui/*.dart + features/auth/auth_widgets.dart   ← Flutter SSOT
        │
        ▼
services/api/lib/matome_api_web/components/matome_components.ex ← HEEx components
services/api/assets/css/components.css                          ← token-only styling
        │
        ▼
THIS notebook  (injects foundations.css + components.css, renders each variant)
        │
        ▼
apps/flutter_widgetbook  (Components/Atoms/*)                   ← Flutter's live render
```

> ### Threat model (read before running)
>
> Livebook executes **arbitrary Elixir** with full OS-user privileges — the
> keys-to-the-kingdom by design. It is therefore **never a dependency of the app
> and never mounted** by the Phoenix router/endpoint. Run it standalone, dev-only:
> `livebook server` then open this file. See `docs/livebook-threat-model.md`.

> **Why this notebook mirrors the class markup (not the compiled components):**
> the HEEx function components need the full app compiled + running, which the
> standalone Livebook does not load. So — exactly like `foundations_catalog.livemd`
> renders swatches from the CSS rather than the app — this catalog emits the SAME
> semantic classes the components produce, over the SAME `components.css`. The
> class contract is the shared surface; the reconciliation note
> (`docs/design-system-reconciliation.md`) records the accepted deviations.

## Load the token + component stylesheets

```elixir
# __DIR__ is services/api/notebooks; the CSS lives one level up under assets.
css_dir = Path.expand("../assets/css", __DIR__)
foundations = File.read!(Path.join(css_dir, "foundations.css"))
components = File.read!(Path.join(css_dir, "components.css"))
css = foundations <> "\n" <> components
IO.puts("Loaded #{byte_size(css)} bytes of tokens + component CSS")
```

## Helpers — icons + the Light/Dark stage

```elixir
# Mirror of matome_components.ex `icon_paths/1` — keep in sync when glyphs change.
icon = fn name, klass ->
  paths =
    case name do
      "check" -> ~s(<path d="M20 6 9 17l-5-5"/>)
      "close" -> ~s(<path d="M18 6 6 18M6 6l12 12"/>)
      "error" -> ~s(<circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 8v4M12 16h.01"/>)
      "add" -> ~s(<path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"/>)
      "cloud_done" ->
        ~s(<path d="M7 18a4 4 0 0 1 0-8 5 5 0 0 1 9.6-1.3A3.5 3.5 0 1 1 17 18Z"/><path d="m9 13 2 2 4-4"/>)
      "cloud_sync" ->
        ~s(<path d="M7 18a4 4 0 0 1 0-8 5 5 0 0 1 9.6-1.3A3.5 3.5 0 1 1 17 18Z"/><path d="M10 12a2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4-1M14 15a2.5 2.5 0 0 1-4 1"/>)
      "cloud_off" ->
        ~s(<path d="M7 18a4 4 0 0 1-.5-8 5 5 0 0 1 7-3.5M17 18a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 1-6.8"/><path d="M3 3l18 18"/>)
      "folder" ->
        ~s(<path d="M3 7a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h4l2 2h6a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v8a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2Z"/>)
      "inbox" ->
        ~s(<path d="M4 13h4l2 3h4l2-3h4"/><path d="M4 13 6 5h12l2 8v5a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H6a2 2 0 0 1-2-2Z"/>)
      "workspaces" ->
        ~s(<circle cx="8" cy="8" r="3"/><circle cx="16" cy="8" r="3"/><circle cx="12" cy="16" r="3"/>)
      "person" -> ~s(<circle cx="12" cy="8" r="4"/><path d="M5 21a7 7 0 0 1 14 0"/>)
      "file" ->
        ~s(<path d="M7 3h7l4 4v13a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H7a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V4a1 1 0 0 1 1-1Z"/><path d="M14 3v4h4"/>)
      "open" ->
        ~s(<path d="M14 4h6v6"/><path d="M20 4 11 13"/><path d="M10 4H6a2 2 0 0 0-2 2v12a2 2 0 0 0 2 2h12a2 2 0 0 0 2-2v-4"/>)
      _ -> ~s(<circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/>)
    end

  ~s(<svg class="matome-icon #{klass}" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" ) <>
    ~s(stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">#{paths}</svg>)
end

# Render one demo `body` (HTML string) on both a Light and a Dark themed stage.
stage = fn css, body ->
  panel = fn label, theme_class ->
    """
    <section class="#{theme_class}" style="flex:1;background:var(--matome-background);
             padding:var(--matome-space-lg);border-radius:var(--matome-radius-lg)">
      <h4 style="margin:0 0 var(--matome-space-md);font:600 var(--matome-type-label-size)/1.25
          var(--matome-font-body);letter-spacing:var(--matome-type-label-tracking);
          text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--matome-text-muted)">#{label}</h4>
      <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:var(--matome-space-md);align-items:flex-start">
        #{body}
      </div>
    </section>
    """
  end

  HTML.new("""
  <style>#{css}</style>
  <div style="display:flex;gap:var(--matome-space-md)">
    #{panel.("Light", "")}
    #{panel.("Dark", "dark")}
  </div>
  """)
end
```

## Buttons — primary / text / icon / submit

```elixir
stage.(css, """
<button class="matome-btn matome-btn--primary">Save</button>
<button class="matome-btn matome-btn--primary">#{icon.("add", "")}<span>Add item</span></button>
<button class="matome-btn matome-btn--primary" disabled>Disabled</button>
<button class="matome-btn matome-btn--text">Cancel</button>
<button class="matome-btn matome-btn--text" disabled>Disabled</button>
<button class="matome-icon-btn" aria-label="Close">#{icon.("close", "")}</button>
<div style="width:100%"></div>
<div style="width:220px"><button class="matome-btn matome-btn--submit">Sign in</button></div>
<div style="width:220px"><button class="matome-btn matome-btn--submit" disabled>
  <span class="matome-spinner matome-spinner--sm"></span></button></div>
""")
```

## Form fields — text / password / select / checkbox

```elixir
stage.(css, """
<div style="width:240px"><label class="matome-field">
  <span class="matome-field__label">Email</span>
  <input class="matome-field__control" type="text" placeholder="you@example.com" value="ana@acme.co">
</label></div>
<div style="width:240px"><label class="matome-field">
  <span class="matome-field__label">Password</span>
  <input class="matome-field__control" type="password" value="secret">
</label></div>
<div style="width:240px"><label class="matome-field">
  <span class="matome-field__label">Disabled</span>
  <input class="matome-field__control" type="text" value="Locked" disabled>
</label></div>
<div style="width:240px"><label class="matome-field">
  <span class="matome-field__label">Space</span>
  <select class="matome-field__control"><option>Work</option><option selected>Personal</option></select>
</label></div>
<label class="matome-checkbox"><input class="matome-checkbox__box" type="checkbox" checked>
  <span>Remember me</span></label>
""")
```

## Feedback — empty state / spinner / banners

```elixir
stage.(css, """
<div style="width:260px"><div class="matome-empty">
  <div class="matome-empty__icon">#{icon.("inbox", "")}</div>
  <div class="matome-empty__title">Nothing here yet</div>
  <div class="matome-empty__message">Add your first item to get started.</div>
</div></div>
<div style="display:flex;gap:var(--matome-space-md);align-items:center">
  <span class="matome-spinner matome-spinner--sm"></span>
  <span class="matome-spinner matome-spinner--md"></span>
  <span class="matome-spinner matome-spinner--lg"></span>
</div>
<div style="width:100%"></div>
<div style="width:300px"><div class="matome-banner matome-banner--error">
  #{icon.("error", "matome-banner__icon")}<span>Invalid credentials.</span></div></div>
<div style="width:300px"><div class="matome-banner matome-banner--notice">
  #{icon.("check", "matome-banner__icon")}<span>Reset link sent.</span></div></div>
""")
```

## Avatars — sizes / icon / people cluster

```elixir
stage.(css, """
<span class="matome-avatar matome-avatar--sm">AK</span>
<span class="matome-avatar matome-avatar--md">AK</span>
